{"title":"Northstar Pet Nutrition","sub":"The CEO blames freight. Is she right?","type":"Profitability","industry":"Pet food manufacturing","geo":"Canada","diff":3,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Hypothesis testing · mix vs inflation · pricing","prompt":"Northstar makes dry dog and cat food sold in Canadian pet stores and supermarkets. Volume grew 9% last year, but operating profit fell from $16.0M to $9.6M. The CEO believes the cause is freight: trucking rates rose sharply. She has asked you to confirm it and recommend a fix.","clarify":[{"q":"Products?","a":"Two recipe families: Classic and Premium (grain-free, higher meat content). Both sell at the same shelf price, about $18 a bag."},{"q":"Why the same price?","a":"Premium was launched at the Classic price two years ago to win shelf space quickly."},{"q":"Freight?","a":"Trucking rates rose about 10% last year."},{"q":"Objective?","a":"Recover last year's profit within 18 months."}],"structure":{"root":"What explains the $6.4M profit fall?","branches":[{"head":"Revenue","items":["Bags sold","Price per bag","Promotions"]},{"head":"Variable cost per bag","items":["Ingredients (by recipe)","Packaging","Freight","Trade promotions"]},{"head":"Mix","items":["Classic vs Premium share","Margin by recipe"]},{"head":"Fixed costs","items":["Plant, marketing, overheads"]}]},"hypothesis":"Freight is a real increase, but it's usually a small share of cost per bag. With two recipes at one price, I suspect a mix shift towards Premium, which costs more to make.","questions":[{"q":"Here is cost per bag. Test the CEO's freight theory.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"388.46pt\" height=\"192.5pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 388.46 192.5\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 192.5 L 388.46 192.5 L 388.46 0 L 0