:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(92.39666 32.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\" d=\"M 1696 0 L 1120 0 L 2829 4006 L 922 4006 L 922 3174 L 442 3174 L 442 4467 L 3373 4467 L 3373 3994 L 1696 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(175.16221 139.222888) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(257.92776 134.726975) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_17\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(340.69331 143.718801) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"legend_1\"><g id=\"patch_13\"><path d=\"M 42.5 18.6 L 58.5 18.6 L 58.5 13 L 42.5 13 z\n\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"text_18\"><g transform=\"translate(64.9 18.6) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-29\" d=\"M 3034 0 L 595 0 L 595 4467 L 1133 4467 L 1133 474 L 3034 474 L 3034 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-1c\" d=\"M 1779 1056 L 2579 3302 L 3085 3302 L 1606 -768 Q 1536 -966 1449 -1078 Q 1363 -1190 1222 -1235 Q 1082 -1280 838 -1280 L 576 -1280 L 576 -832 L 1094 -832 L 1344 -128 L 109 3302 L 621 3302 L 1414 1056 L 1568 518 L 1600 518 L 1779 1056 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-29\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1\" transform=\"translate(50 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-16\" transform=\"translate(103.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-17\" transform=\"translate(151.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e9\" transform=\"translate(186.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1c\" transform=\"translate(210.09375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-6\" transform=\"translate(259.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1\" transform=\"translate(314.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-15\" transform=\"translate(367.8125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"patch_14\"><path d=\"M 113.26125 18.6 L 129.26125 18.6 L 129.26125 13 L 113.26125 13 z\n\" style=\"fill: #c2410c\"/></g><g id=\"text_19\"><g transform=\"translate(135.66125 18.6) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-31\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-b\" transform=\"translate(57.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-c\" transform=\"translate(114 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-16\" transform=\"translate(139 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e9\" transform=\"translate(187.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1c\" transform=\"translate(211.296875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-6\" transform=\"translate(260.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1\" transform=\"translate(315.609375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-15\" transform=\"translate(369.015625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p4737636fa4\"><rect x=\"35.3\" y=\"28\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"138.6\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Cost per bag ($)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Cost per bag rose $1.54. Freight is only +$0.15 of that, worth $0.65M on 4.35M bags: <b>10% of the $6.40M gap</b>.</p> <p>Ingredients rose $1.14 a bag, worth $4.96M: <b>77% of the gap</b>.</p> <p>Full bridge: more bags +$2.80M, higher cost per bag −$6.70M, higher fixed costs −$2.50M: −$6.40M in total. Volume growth roughly offsets the fixed-cost rise, so cost per bag is the story.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> freight is real but minor. Ingredients are the story. Let's see why they rose.</p>","note":"Both years: price $18 per bag. Bags: 4.00M → 4.35M. Fixed costs: $16.0M → $18.5M."},{"q":"Here is ingredient cost by recipe and the recipe mix. Split the ingredient increase into inflation and mix.","exhibit":{"kind":"table","headers":["","Classic","Premium"],"rows":[["Ingredient cost per bag, last year ($)","5.50","9.00"],["Ingredient cost per bag, this year ($)","5.80","10.20"],["Share of bags, last year","80%","20%"],["Share of bags, this year","65%","35%"]],"title":"Exhibit 2 · Ingredients by recipe","note":null,"align":["l","r","r"],"boldLast":false},"answer":"<p><b>Mix effect</b> (more Premium at last year's costs): (35% − 20%) × ($9.00 − 5.50) = <b>$0.525</b> a bag.</p> <p><b>Inflation</b> (each recipe got dearer): 65% × $0.30 + 35% × $1.20 = <b>$0.615</b> a bag.</p> <p>Total $1.14 ✓. Mix and inflation are roughly half each.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> Premium is succeeding with shoppers, but it earns $4.40 less per bag than Classic because it's sold at the same price. Northstar is growing its least profitable product.</p>"},{"q":"If Northstar raised only the Premium price, how much more per bag would it need to recover the full gap? Is that realistic?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Premium bags: 35% × 4.35M = 1.52M. Needed: $6.40M ÷ 1.52M = <b>$4.20 a bag</b>, about 23% on $18, assuming volume holds.</p> <p>Probably too much in one go. Premium recipes usually sell at a clear premium to standard ones, so some increase is justified, but a 23% jump risks losing shelf space.</p> <p><b>Better:</b> a $2 to $3 increase on Premium (it's still a better product), plus ingredient sourcing contracts, plus cutting trade promotions that rose $0.15 a bag.</p>"},{"q":"What would you tell the CEO in her board meeting?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Answer first: freight explains only about 10% of the fall. The real issue is that Premium, now 35% of volume, is priced like Classic while costing $4.40 more in ingredients. Then: the pricing fix, sourcing, and a test of price elasticity in one region.</p>"}],"reco":"Freight is not the main problem: it explains about 10% of the $6.4M profit fall. Most of the gap comes from ingredients, split between inflation and a shift to Premium, which sells at the Classic price but costs $4.40 more a bag to make. I recommend repricing Premium by $2 to $3 a bag, locking in ingredient contracts, and trimming trade promotions. Risk: retailers resist a price rise, so lead with the stronger recipe story. Next step: test the new Premium price in one province for eight weeks.","great":["Tests the client's hypothesis with numbers instead of accepting it","Splits ingredients into mix and inflation","Spots the pricing decision behind the mix problem","Sizes the price fix and judges whether it's realistic"],"id":26,"slug":"northstar-pet-nutrition"}